* BAT54 - Schottky barrier diode, SOT23, Diodes Incorporated (30 V, 200 mA)
* Model: the manufacturer's own file, BAT54.spice.txt (a Zetex model, v1.0, last
*   revised 25/04/00), served at https://www.diodes.com/spice/download/510/BAT54.spice.txt
*   obtained 2026-10-28; vendor original frozen at vendor/diodes/diodes_inc/BAT54/BAT54.spice.txt
*   (sha256 a1d142e1f32ea55aca3aa434897a3b648266f58b91745aa79579640b52eccd03).
* Datasheet checked against: DS11005 Rev. 34-2 (Nov. 2023), vendor/diodes/diodes_inc/BAT54/BAT54_A_C_S_DS11005.pdf.
* Instantiate: Dxxx anode cathode BAT54      (model name BAT54, as served)
*
* Verdict against the datasheet (scripts/validate_models.py, set temp = 25):
*   V_F 141/208/301/385/584 mV at 0.1/1/10/30/100 mA against max 240/320/400/500/800: inside.
*   I_R 0.763 uA at V_R = 25 V, 25 C against max 2 uA: inside, but 3.7x the typical curve (Fig. 2, ~0.2 uA).
*   C_T 7.63 pF at V_R = 1 V against max 10 pF (Fig. 3 typical read ~9.3 pF: 18% low); 2.53 pF at 25 V (fig. ~2.6).
*   I_R(T): 0.76 / 7.07 / 17.3 / 226 uA at 25 / 60 / 75 / 125 C. The temperature rise (x9.3 from 25 to 60 C)
*   follows Fig. 2 (x9.5) but the whole curve sits ~3.4x above the typical one: the leakage is IS = 649 nA, flat
*   in V_R, with XTI = 2, EG = 0.58. Use it as a bounded estimate (typical x3.4), not as the typical part.
* Not modelled / to know: no KF/AF; IKF, ISR, NR are used by ngspice's diode model and appear in its dump;
* leakage does not rise with V_R as Fig. 2 does. Vendor disclaimer follows unaltered.
